+ * M1 (0264): the modem pool, 16 MB of RAM XNU does not manage at 0x89000000 (Linux System RAM
+ *   88f00000-8aafffff; nothing uses it once the shim has jumped), write-combined; one 4 KB page
+ *   of it goes HLOS -> {HLOS, MSS_MSA} -> HLOS through hyp_assign and is read and written after
+ *   each step (plan stage 3; argument layout from ios-topaz 0121 scm_assign_to_modem). Rails and
+ *   clocks wait for the boot itself.
  * SMEM structures and lookups from ios-topaz TopazModem.cpp (0113), plus the v11 global heap.
  * SMEM is mapped write-combined (Normal NC): no cache upkeep, unaligned reads are fine.
